# Source-method review

Inspected experiment-repo revision 07234686ab41ec3071299924d8ee10b1edf38377: analysis/estimate_pi.py, analysis/README.md, and the unchanged brief. The analysis owner's reply in experiment-repo#4 explicitly leaves numeric results pending; that request remains open.

The code implements all required sample sizes and 50 runs per size with seed 2026+i, i=0,...,49. A fresh generator draws (N,2) uniform arrays, counts x²+y² <= 1, and computes 4K/N. It averages absolute errors against math.pi. The requested natural-log least-squares fit has an intercept and a correctly implemented centered-slope cross-check. Repeated seeds across N create the documented nested pairing. The optional bootstrap resamples complete run-index triplets, preserving that pairing, and its vectorized slope expression correctly cancels the intercept. The theoretical variance and asymptotic absolute-error formulas in the README are correct.

No source-method defect found. This is not verification of generated numbers or approval of a delivered report: results, provenance and the assembled report still require inspection.
